        "original_id": "48248b62-3778-59e8-899b-ecad215d4f65",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Double\n- Products: Blue, Dou3le, \"The Captain of Her Heart\", \"Devils Ball\", \"Woman of the World\", \"Rangoon Moon\"\n- Places: Europe\n- Concepts: hit singles, album releases\n\nFacts:\n- Double was a Swiss music duo pronounced \"doo-blay.\"\n- In 1986, Double released \"The Captain of Her Heart\" as a single, and it became an immediate success throughout Europe.\n- \"The Captain of Her Heart\" was an international smash hit by Double and is a plaintive, atmospheric, piano-led ballad.\n- The album Blue included updated versions of Double's earlier singles \"Woman of the World\" and \"Rangoon Moon.\"\n- Double was best known for its hit single \"The Captain of Her Heart.\"\n- \"Devils Ball\" is a song by Double that was released as the lead single from the duo's second studio album Dou3le.",
